    <span class="c1">// Manually manage the child VC's life cycle</span>
    <span class="k">return</span> <span class="nb">NO</span><span class="p">;</span>
<span class="p">}</span>
</pre></td></tr></tbody></table></code></pre></div></div>

<p>However, note that you must not call methods like <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">viewWillAppear</code> or <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">viewDidAppear</code> manually. Instead, you should call:</p>

<div class="language-objc highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><table class="rouge-table"><tbody><tr><td class="rouge-gutter gl"><pre class="lineno">1
2
</pre></td><td class="rouge-code"><pre><span class="k">-</span> <span class="p">(</span><span class="kt">void</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="nf">beginAppearanceTransition</span><span class="p">:(</span><span class="n">BOOL</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="nv">isAppearing</span> <span class="nf">animated</span><span class="p">:(</span><span class="n">BOOL</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="nv">animated</span><span class="p">;</span>
<span class="k">-</span> <span class="p">(</span><span class="kt">void</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="n">endAppearanceTransition</span><span class="p">;</span>
</pre></td></tr></tbody></table></code></pre></div></div>

<blockquote>
  <p>Note: <em><strong>use these two methods to indirectly trigger the child controller’s life cycle, and they must be used in pairs</strong></em></p>
