<h4 id="common-transition-animation">Common transition animation</h4>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">transitionFromViewController:toViewController:duration:options:animations:completion:</code> is the “officially recommended” way for a custom container controller to switch between two child controllers. It automatically forwards the appearance life cycle (<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">viewWill</code>/<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">DidAppear</code>/<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Disappear</code>) for you, so you don’t need to manually call <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">beginAppearanceTransition</code>/<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">endAppearanceTransition</code>.</p>

<p>A minimal working pattern (fromVC is the currently displayed child controller, toVC is the child controller you’re switching to):</p>

